from pathlib import Path
p=Path('help/index.html');s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');needle='<section><h2>Inspect dynamic controls</h2>'
assert needle in s
addition='''<section><h2>Inspect responsive layout rules</h2><p>Open a project and choose <strong>Layout rules</strong> in the upper-right page selector. Select a component to read captured Align, Anchors, geometry, serialized parent, margins, padding, constraints, autosizing, wrapping, DPI and resize events with source evidence.</p><p>Scroll the command bar horizontally to reach <strong>Parent width change</strong>, <strong>Parent height change</strong> and <strong>Apply example</strong>. Enter positive or negative whole numbers from -10000 to 10000 and apply. Invalid input preserves the previous valid example. Applying refreshes the filter and returns to the first page. Numeric examples require explicit Align=None and recognized anchors on an ordinary child with a captured parent. Active alignment, inheritance and missing or unknown rules remain qualified.</p><p>Filter by component or explanation. Next page advances through 250 components; First page resets. Drag the divider and scroll the detail box. Component source requires attached unchanged text; detached, changed and binary locations are refused. Examples show basic changes, not absolute final geometry. Constraints, sibling allocation, defaults, custom code and DPI can alter actual behavior. Compare Object Inspector settings and resize the target separately.</p><p>Full steps: <code>docs/guides/Layout_Rules_Run_and_Test.txt</code>. Developers: run <code>tools/build-layout-rules.cmd</code> elevated for 56 focused checks.</p></section>'''
s=s.replace(needle,addition+needle,1);p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
